{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1772650939,"nonce":"Mkzlz4fGEUFnUE8bCmeu7uDCkkE=","title":"git-bug lock contention when concurrent processes access the same repo","message":"git-bug uses a lock file (`\u003crepo\u003e/.git/git-bug/lock`) and fails with a non-zero exit code when two concurrent processes attempt operations on the same repo simultaneously.\n\n**Observed:** Mandible issue-scanner runs `git-bug bug ls` / `git-bug bug show` via `spawnSync` on a periodic schedule. When Claude Code or another agent also runs git-bug commands on the same repo at the same time, one of them may fail due to lock contention. `runGitBug()` in `issue-scanner.ts` checks `if (result.status !== 0) { return null; }` — so a lock-contention failure silently returns null rather than retrying.\n\n**Fix options:**\n1. Add retry with backoff in `runGitBug()` for lock-contention exits\n2. Serialize all git-bug access through a single queue in Mandible\n\n**Status:** Fixed in dotfiles retro-fixes branch. This issue tracks the fix landing in the standalone repo.\n\nMigrated from dotfiles issue e139954.","files":null}]}